  "excluded": "Hosted triggers, schedulers, operational SQL, captured data and blanket grants are deliberately excluded. Local bootstrap supplies constraints, RLS and ownership separately. Cluster aggregate must use a scoped invoker view rather than an unscoped materialized-view grant.",
  "localDifferences": [
    "Local queue admits snapshot refresh and installation-owner achievement evaluation only",
    "Snapshot refresh uses a dedicated non-login non-bypass role",
    "Authenticated snapshot reads follow local guild membership",
    "No hosted schedulers, triggers, game credentials or captured state",
    "Selected core analytic definers use the non-login, non-bypass read owner. Catalogue tables allow authenticated reads only, with no public caller writes. Comprehensive player statistics remain service-only behind the canonical application authorization path.",
    "Local workspace recovery stores a digest only; code provisioning requires the current password and reset targets only the installation account.",
    "Empty file workspaces admit desktop_local_claim attestations without an upstream invitation. These represent local labels only, with automatic game sync disabled; they cannot establish upstream account ownership.",
    "A dedicated non-login non-bypass importer commits only the setup subject's guild and matching cluster, reads only raid conflict-key columns, and stores owner-scoped receipts. Caller roles cannot invoke the import primitive or inspect receipts.",
    "Meta-team memberships retain canonical rows and timestamps, scoped reads, own self declarations and same-guild leader overrides; local clients cannot write automated reconciler records.",
    "An own-key roster snapshot remains an explicit unverified local claim. A dedicated non-login non-bypass writer atomically commits its bounded cache, canonical mapped rows and local power; renderer roles cannot write cached payloads or invoke the primitive.",
    "Authenticated local planner-link writes use the canonical owner-only projection and a bounded HTTP(S) write validator; role, identity and credential columns stay read-only. Historical links and unrelated profile updates are retained while future link writes are checked.",
    "Canonical achievement inputs include guild-war attempts and computed raid awards. Owner-readable first-unlock rows are written by a strict durable local job; award calculation uses a non-login non-bypass reader scoped to the requesting installation. Guild-war input writes and module acquisition remain outside this selected closure."
  ]
